					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aismallard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4598089); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4598089&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200778" alt="aismallard" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4598089)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aismallard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4598089); return false;" >aismallard</a></span> <span class="odate time_1565842758 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Aug 2019 04:19</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4331040">
									

<p>Pretty good, liked the story of the Ethics Committee doing its thing. I do have some minor nitpicks about the piece:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Operation Black Dove. (See Addendum 4263-1.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think &quot;Black Dove (see Addendum 4263-1).&quot; looks cleaner.</p>
<p>There are breaks every time you introduce an image due to the way Wikidot joins quoteblocks. You can have them all in one block if you use a <tt><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[div]]</span></tt> instead, styled appropriately. (See <a href="http://scptestwiki.wikidot.com/sigma:quote-blocks">here</a>).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mr. Danton begin his work with the Foundation as an agent recruited out of the United States Military,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The US military doesn't really have &quot;agents&quot;, &quot;officer&quot; probably makes more sense here. It would also make sense to specify a specific branch, given how large they are and the differences they have in organizational culture.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The previous log was a call from Junior Researcher Alan Raleigh, who had recently been assigned to Site-36. Yes, I know we said it was an anonymous. Yes, that was a lie. We find it helps people find the will to report things.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I mean, I figured this was probably true, but wouldn't this be 5/ETHICS classified? Like confidential informants are a thing; just having the Committee member say what we all expected is a bit jarring. You could keep the dialogue the same by just calling them &quot;John Doe&quot; in-universe for privacy and the narrative effect would be the same.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

